<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    PASTE THE PLAY CONSOLE IDS HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE.

    Every one of these is the opaque id Google assigns a leaderboard, of the
    form CgkI...  The game itself never sees them: index.html sends a logical
    name and Boards.kt maps it here, so ids can be reissued or a whole game
    re-created in the console without the web layer being touched.

    An entry left empty means "not configured". The bridge logs and declines
    rather than calling the SDK with a blank id, so a half-configured build
    runs fine and simply has fewer boards.

    tools/gpg-boards.js creates all thirty-five over the Play Games
    Publishing API and prints them in exactly this format.
-->
